{"format":"megamek-board","version":2,"size":{"width":63,"height":84},"name":"Road Grades - Concrete","description":"Matched road grading specimens. Three panels, left to right: road only, centered rail, beside rail. Each panel has the same 34 annotated cases in three columns, read left to right then down. The first six rows rotate straight, gentle 60-degree, and sharp 120-degree roads through all six directions. The middle rises or falls 1, 2, or 3 levels. Rails bypass a sharp road bend with two legal gentle pieces. Further rows contain mixed-height T/X junctions, raised and lowered bridge banks, a curved deck, an overpass, explicit cliffs, a deep cut and flat/sloped concrete aprons. The final six ordinary cases add continuous inclines, inside corner cut/fill, a rail placement transition and a graded bent bridge. Beside placement applies only to actual shared corridor sides. The first 28 cases deliberately stress geometry; their steep heights do not imply that every vehicle can traverse them. Inspect in Classic and Enhanced, from above and both oblique directions. Cell labels and exact serialized topology are in the CSV manifest.","options":{"exitRoadsToPavement":false},"tags":["Example"],"notes":[{"at":[4,4],"text":["Road only / straight-0","straight from N; middle +1 levels"]},{"at":[11,4],"text":["Road only / straight-1","straight from NE; middle -2 levels"]},{"at":[18,4],"text":["Road only / straight-2","straight from SE; middle +3 levels"]},{"at":[25,4],"text":["Road and centered rail / straight-0","straight from N; middle +1 levels"]},{"at":[32,4],"text":["Road and centered rail / straight-1","straight from NE; middle -2 levels"]},{"at":[39,4],"text":["Road and centered rail / straight-2","straight from SE; middle +3 levels"]},{"at":[46,4],"text":["Road and beside rail / straight-0","straight from N; middle +1 levels"]},{"at":[53,4],"text":["Road and beside rail / straight-1","straight from NE; middle -2 levels"]},{"at":[60,4],"text":["Road and beside rail / 